<title>FRANCE: Air France to add 747 combi to cargo fleet.</title>
<headline>Air France to add 747 combi to cargo fleet.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-09-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Air France said an additional Boeing 747-200 freighter aircraft will join its fleet from February 1997.</p>
<p>&quot;The aircraft, a 747-200 combi, is currently being converted to full-cargo configuration in our workshops  and will take our 747-200 freighter fleet to 12,&quot; an Air France cargo official told Reuters.</p>
<p>The converted combi will enable Air France to operate extra freighter flights, in particular, to Miami and Chicago, from March next year, the official said. --Air Cargo Newsroom Tel+44 171 542 7706 Fax +44 171 542 5017</p>
